    [BugFix] Correct GBSA static kernel blacklist name (#19317)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Correct the GBSA static-kernel blacklist entry introduced by #18869 from
    `GenericBlockSparseAttn` to `GenericBlockSparseAttention`. npugraph_ex
    matches blacklist entries against JSON filenames by substring, so the
    old spelling does not exclude the actual CANN operator. MiniMax-M3 can
    consequently execute an incompatible static GBSA kernel and fail with an
    AI Core buffer-out-of-bounds error during graph capture.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. The intended GBSA exclusion now takes effect when static kernel
    compilation is enabled. TopKV2 and the other entries are unchanged. This
    PR changes one string on one line.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Manual A3 regression: MiniMax-M3 W8A8, TP4 x DP4, MRV2, EAGLE3=3, CANN
    9.2.0; `enable_npugraph_ex`, `enable_static_kernel`, and
    `enable_super_kernel` all true. Runtime baseline: main
    `bc078fc954cd9a14c8c1d4da54ea2b28ac34d363` plus PR18426 head
    `1ebea6843b79e91f7a88d270f3460e5bff79516a` to use CANN GBSA.
    - Before: startup failed at the first graph-capture bucket with a
    `static_kernel_GenericBlockSparseAttention` AI Core error. After
    changing only this blacklist string: both 17-bucket capture phases
    completed, all 16 workers finished graph capture, all four DP ranks
    logged super-kernel enablement, and HTTP health returned 200.
    - Simple and 4,383-token chat requests returned the expected answers
    (`400` and `739251`). 272 GBSA JSON files were excluded, with no GBSA in
    the selected compile inputs. Existing nonfatal MsaIndexScore
    static-compilation failures remain; this change does not fix them.
    - Focused Ruff lint/format checks and `git diff --check` passed. The
    local full pre-commit run did not complete; full repository checks are
    running in Linux CI. No new test file: validation used the hardware
    startup regression above. GPQA was not rerun.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
